          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Founding the Wright Company</strong><br>\nIn 1909, the Wright brothers formed the Wright Company, which manufactured airplanes on a larger scale. They also opened a pilot training school. The company prospered as aviation technology became more sought after, especially for its military applications during World War I.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Years and Legacy</strong><br>\nAfter Wilbur's death from typhoid fever in 1912, Orville continued their work but eventually sold the company in 1915. He remained active in aeronautics, serving on various boards and committees. The brothers' legacy continued to inspire others, and they are credited with laying the groundwork for modern aviation.</p>\n\n<p><strong>The Wright Brothers' Enduring Impact</strong><br>\nToday, the Wright brothers are remembered as the fathers of modern flight. They not only built and flew the first powered aircraft but also developed the fundamental principles of control that made the future of aviation possible. Their pioneering spirit continues to influence and propel the aerospace industry forward.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
